course: dictionary
lesson: 16174
title: An old word for made or caused
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Wrought» is an old past form of the verb «work». It means made, shaped or caused. You will mostly meet it in old books, history and formal writing.
explain: «The storm wrought great damage on the village.» The storm did not work on the village like a job. It caused the damage. When you swap in «caused», the sentence still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: Look at the words near «wrought» to find clues. In «wrought iron», iron has been heated and hammered into shape. In «overwrought», the word «over» and the sentence about being upset tell you the person is very worked up or nervous.
fact: «Wrought» is an old past form of «work», meaning made, shaped or caused.
fact: «Wrought iron» is iron that has been heated and hammered into shape, used for gates, railings and fences.
fact: «Wrought havoc» means caused great damage.
fact: «Overwrought» means very upset, nervous or worked up.
fact: «Finely wrought» means skilfully made.
exercise: «The storm wrought great damage on the village.» What does wrought mean here? | Counted carefully | Painted bright colours | Ran away from | * Caused
exercise: «The old gate was made of wrought iron and had curly patterns.» What is wrought iron? | Paint on a wall | * Iron heated and hammered into shape | Glass in a window | Soft plastic
exercise: Mum says, «I am overwrought, the bus is late again.» What does overwrought mean? | * Very upset or worked up | Very quiet | Calm and sleepy | Happy to wait
test: «The flood wrought havoc across the farm.» What does wrought havoc mean? | Brought a rainbow | * Caused great damage | Made a new field | Dried up the rivers
test: «The silver box was finely wrought, with tiny leaves carved all over it.» What does finely wrought mean? | Dusty and old | Painted in one colour | Lost and broken | * Skilfully made
exam: «She was so overwrought that she could not sleep.» What does overwrought suggest? | Bright and cheerful | Very rested and calm | * Very upset and nervous | Sleepy and bored
